  "highlight": "Karen Throsby crossed the English Channel from England to France in 16 hours 9 minutes on 2 September 2010.",
  "biography": [
    "Throsby reached Pointe du Riden, south of Cap Gris-Nez, in September 2010. A sociologist as well as a marathon swimmer, she later wrote Immersion: Marathon Swimming, Embodiment and Identity, published by Manchester University Press in 2016.",
    "The English Channel swim on 2 September 2010 took 16 hours 9 minutes. The Catalina federation records 14 hours 11 minutes 52 seconds on 20 July 2011. In New York the 24 August 2013 Manhattan circuit took 8 hours 41 minutes 1 seconds."
